findings.root_cause:
Every element in every outpost pool is emitted with projection "rigid" — the value is hardcoded in the shared element() builder, so there is no way for any pool to be anything else. In JigsawPlacement.Placer.tryPlacingChildren the placement Y is chosen by:

    if (sourceRigid && targetRigid) { targetBoxY = sourceBoxY + deltaY; }
    else { sourceJigsawBaseHeight = chunkGenerator.getFirstFreeHeight(sourceJigsawPos.getX(), sourceJigsawPos.getZ(), Heightmap.Types.WORLD_SURFACE_WG, ...); targetBoxY = sourceJigsawBaseHeight - targetJigsawLocalY; }

Because every element is rigid, the first branch is taken for EVERY connection in the whole structure. The terrain is consulted exactly once, in JigsawStructure.findGenerationPoint -> JigsawPlacement.addPieces, for the START piece only (bottomY = position.getY() + getFirstFreeHeight(centreX, centreZ, WORLD_SURFACE_WG)). After that the entire fan is pure algebra chained off forge_hall's Y. A building 60-90 blocks away is placed at the start island's deck altitude no matter what is (or is not) under it.

This is precisely the thing vanilla avoids. In village/plains, town_centers and houses are "rigid" but streets.json and terminators.json are "terrain_matching" — the connective tissue re-grounds every branch on the local heightmap, and the rigid houses hang off an already-regrounded street. pillager_outpost does the same with feature_plates.json ("terrain_matching") carrying rigid features.json cages/tents. The mod has zero terrain_matching elements anywhere.

On the Hollow Horizon this is fatal rather than merely untidy: terrain = max(min(caves, chasms), sky_islands) (gen_worldgen.py:1146), and WORLD_SURFACE_WG returns the top of a SKY island when one is overhead. Sky islands live at roughly y166-220 (from SKY_TOP_FROM/SKY_BOTTOM_* at gen_worldgen.py:325-328) while Resonant Plains mainland tops out around y66-155. So the start piece frequently lands on a sky island top, and the 96-block fan then walks straight off the island edge and hangs 60-150 blocks over the mainland.

