corrected_fix:
Stop hardcoding the material in the bank calculation; read the stack's own ATTACK_DAMAGE modifier so any subclass or material is automatically correct.

In C:/Projects/The Echoing Void/src/main/java/com/echoingvoid/item/HarmonicSwordItem.java replace lines 141-143:

    private static float attackDamage(ItemStack stack) {
        return (float) stack
            .getOrDefault(DataComponents.ATTRIBUTE_MODIFIERS, ItemAttributeModifiers.EMPTY)
            .compute(Attributes.ATTACK_DAMAGE, 0.0D, EquipmentSlot.MAINHAND);
    }

(`ItemAttributeModifiers.compute(Holder<Attribute>, double, EquipmentSlot)` is ItemAttributeModifiers.java:87; `EMPTY` is line 37. This picks up the ADD_VALUE modifier that createSwordAttributes installs at ToolMaterial.java:99-103, so harmonic_sword yields 5.5 exactly as today and knell_sword correctly yields 8.5. It also picks up Sharpness-style attribute modifiers if the stack has any, which is arguably more faithful to "what a swing is worth"; if that is unwanted, keep the static form but make it non-static/protected and override it in KnellSwordItem to return `3.0F + KnellMaterials.KNELL.attackDamageBonus()`.)

Minimal alternative if the attribute-reading version is rejected: change `private static float attackDamage(ItemStack stack)` to `protected float attackDamage(ItemStack stack)` and add to KnellSwordItem.java:

    @Override
    protected float attackDamage(ItemStack stack) {
        return 3.0F + KnellMaterials.KNELL.attackDamageBonus();
    }

Either way the ATTACK_BASELINE constant and the ModKnell.java:153 literal 3.0F should be unified so a future material swap cannot drift again. No change is needed to the `use`/`hurtEnemy` hooks themselves — those are correct as written.
